# Allowed signers for the preflight attestation (see .github/workflows/pr.yml).
#
# Format is what `ssh-keygen -Y verify` and `git` (gpg.format=ssh) read: one
# entry per line,
#
#   <principal> <keytype> <base64 key>
#
# The principal is the `comment` field of the local signing key, so a key
# committed here must match the principal the signer used. Lines starting with
# `#` are comments. One key with several principals is space-separated.
#
# Add every machine allowed to attest a preflight run:
#
#   cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
#
# No real key is committed here: the signing keys live on the local machines
# (the sandboxed agents have none), so this is a placeholder until the
# orchestrator adds them. Until then no attestation verifies, and CI runs the
# tests (fail-closed).
